In one dimension, oscillator operators are linked via relations akin to those of the CGLS theorem, which include integral operators known as intertwining operators. This study examines integral representations for eigeneigenvectors of the oscillators, thereby deriving explicit formulas for the oscillators themselves, which factorize into products of a Laguerre integral kernel and a universal constant. Furthermore, it is established an analog of the CGLS theorem valid for a pair of oscillators in a context.
